      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T23:49:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Small suggestion: would it be OK to keep the existing checks here and in `dma_buf_mmap_internal()`, and only replace `vma_pages()` with `vma_kernel_pages()`? Something like:\n\n```\n    /* check for offset overflow */\n    if (pgoff + vma_kernel_pages(vma) \u003c pgoff)\n        return -EOVERFLOW;\n\n    /* check for overflowing the buffer\u0027s size */\n    if (pgoff + vma_kernel_pages(vma) \u003e\n        dmabuf-\u003esize \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT)\n        return -EINVAL;\n```\n\nAs far as I can see, `vma_kernel_pages()` is never larger than `vma_pages()`, so the sums can\u0027t wrap where they didn\u0027t before. The `dma-buf.c` change would come down to three lines, and importers would keep getting `-EOVERFLOW` for a wrapping `pgoff`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "6ef37ec70efe21caf75d5df8885b5cfdd466b4b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
